# SRG-APP-000089-AU-000400  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must be configured to retain the DoW-defined
# attributes of the log records sent by the devices and hosts.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000089-AU-000400
group:           V-206453
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000169
control_rev5:    AU-12

contribution:    Splunk retains the raw record verbatim and stamps index-time attributes on
                 it: the destination index and sourcetype assigned per data input, and the
                 event time derived by the timestamp extractor.

governs:         inputs.conf - Configures inputs, distributed inputs such as forwarders, and file system
                 monitoring.
governs:         props.conf - How incoming data is recognized, parsed and timestamped.

check:           inputs.conf [] index non_empty
check:           inputs.conf [] sourcetype non_empty
check:           props.conf [] DATETIME_CONFIG not_in NONE|CURRENT
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          inputs.conf [] index https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.2-configuration-file-reference/inputs.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The DoD/organization-defined attribute list is held in the site security
                 plan; the check text defers to it, so the criterion tests only that Splunk
                 assigns the attributes it controls.
external:        Where field filters are defined, comparing the fields they mask against
                 the organization's attribute list is an inspection against that document,
                 not a condition configuration can decide.

citation:        INVENTION. Removed field_filters.conf [<fieldFilterName>] action not_in
                 "host"=null()|"source"=null()|"sourcetype"=null()|"_time"=null().
                 field_filters.conf.spec defines action as "<field> = <operator>" with
                 "<operator> ::= null() | sha256() | sha512() | <string literal> |
                 sed(<string literal>)", an open value space: sha256(), a replacement
                 literal, or a sed expression on _raw removes or rewrites an attribute just
                 as effectively, and any difference in quoting or spacing evades an
                 exact-match list. The condition yields a confident pass that is not
                 evidence. Field filters also act on search results, not on what the index
                 retains. Stanza placeholders [<input stanza>] and [<spec>] were replaced
                 with the empty stanza the determined rows carry, since assess.sh matches
                 stanza names literally and a placeholder never matches. DATETIME_CONFIG
                 aligned with SRG-APP-000096-AU-000690.
finding:         Splunk does not stamp the index-time attributes it controls on the records
                 in scope - a destination index, a sourcetype, or a recognized event time
                 is missing - so the attributes the organization requires are not retained.
